{"name":"Lei Flower","hex":"#d87b6a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lei","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Lemio."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A garland of flowers in Hawaii."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lei"},{"term":"flower","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colorful, conspicuous structure associated with angiosperms, frequently scented and attracting various insects, and which may or may not be used for sexual reproduction.","A reproductive structure in angiosperms (flowering plants), often conspicuously colourful and typically including sepals, petals, and either or both stamens and/or a pistil."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To put forth blooms.","To decorate with pictures of flowers."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flower"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lei (garland)","blocks":[{"text":"A lei is a garland or wreath, typically consisting of fresh natural foliage, common in Polynesia and the Philippines. More loosely defined, a lei is any series of objects strung together with the intent to be worn. Lei of various styles are given as gifts to honour people throughout the Pacific, being presented, for example, to visiting dignitaries, graduates, or to loved ones who are departing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Lei_pikake.jpg/330px-Lei_pikake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lei_(garland)","wikidata":"Q541357"},{"title":"Flower","blocks":[{"text":"Flowers, also known as blossoms and blooms, are the reproductive structures of flowering plants. Typically, they are structured in four circular levels around the end of a stalk. These include: sepals, which are modified leaves that support the flower; petals, often designed to attract pollinators; male stamens, where pollen is presented; and female gynoecia, where pollen is received and its movement is facilitated to the egg. When flowers are arranged in a group, they are known collectively as an inflorescence."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Magnolia_grandiflora_-_flower_1.jpg/330px-Magnolia_grandiflora_-_flower_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flower","wikidata":"Q506"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Lei_Hulu.jpg/500px-Lei_Hulu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Lei_Hulu.jpg/1280px-Lei_Hulu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Lei_Hulu.jpg/500px-Lei_Hulu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Lei hulu, made from feathers","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALei_Hulu.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Lei_Wili.jpg/500px-Lei_Wili.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Lei_Wili.jpg/1280px-Lei_Wili.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Lei_Wili.jpg/500px-Lei_Wili.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Wili method of making leis","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALei_Wili.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Patsy_Mink_Lyndon_Johnson.jpg/500px-Patsy_Mink_Lyndon_Johnson.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Patsy_Mink_Lyndon_Johnson.jpg/1280px-Patsy_Mink_Lyndon_Johnson.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign